  "body": "The following historical copies of the spec proposals page are currently publicly available:\r\n\r\n* https://spec.matrix.org/v1.1/proposals/\r\n* https://spec.matrix.org/v1.2/proposals/\r\n\r\nThese contain old copies of the proposal listings, with the latter (v1.2) being what users navigate to by default when visiting https://spec.matrix.org and clicking \"Spec Change Proposals\" in the left sidebar.\r\n\r\nIdeally there should only ever be an up-to-date copy of the page available ([/unstable/proposals](https://spec.matrix.org/unstable/proposals)), which users should be directed to when they try to visit any versioned copies of the page. The easiest way to do this as @turt2live proposes is to simply redirect the above listed pages to `/unstable/proposals`.\r\n\r\nBonus points (but please this as well) if while we're messing about with reverse proxy configs if we can instead host the page on `spec.matrix.org/proposals`, as I find that cleaner than `/unstable/proposals`, and makes sense as the page is not intended to be versioned.",
